# Install spin after finishing work

When a task that changes Go code, the CLI, or the TUI is complete (tests/gates done, or the user can run the result):

1. Rebuild with `make -B build`
2. Install with `make install` (`~/.local/bin/spin`)
3. Confirm the installed binary is newer than the source change (mtime or hash)

Do this even if `make test` already compiled `build/bin/spin`. That target does not update `~/.local/bin/spin`.

```bash
make -B build && make install
```

Skip only when the *session* touched no runnable spin code (docs-only, specs-only, promptkit-only). If any earlier step in the same run changed Go/CLI/TUI, still install before yielding — a docs-only last item does not skip.
